    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="register-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">IWB_WDOMAINR&lt;n&gt;, n = 0 - 4095</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">IWB Wire Interrupt Domain Selection Register</p><div data-pagefind-body="1">
        <p>IWB Wire Interrupt Domain Selection Register. Allows software to configure the Interrupt Domain that wires n  16 through ((n  16) + 15) are assigned to.</p>
      </div><h3>Configuration</h3><p>This register is present only when FEAT_GICv5_EXT is implemented. Otherwise, direct accesses to IWB_WDOMAINR&lt;n&gt; are <span class="arm-defined-word">RES0</span>.</p>
        <p>The number of implemented IWB_WDOMAINR&lt;n&gt; registers is (IWB_IDR0.IW_RANGE + 1) * 2.</p>

      
        <p>The effects of a write to this register are not guaranteed to have completed until IWB_WDOMAIN_STATUSR.IDLE is 1.</p>
      <h3>Attributes</h3>
        <p>IWB_WDOMAINR&lt;n&gt; is a 32-bit register.</p>
      <p>This  register is part of the <a href="iwb_config_frame.html">IWB_CONFIG_FRAME</a> block.</p><h2>Field descriptions</h2><table class="regdiagram" id="fieldset_0"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM15</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM14</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM13</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM12</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM11</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM10</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM9</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM8</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM7</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM6</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM5</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM4</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM3</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM2</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM1</a></td><td class="lr" colspan="2"><a href="#fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM0</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="fieldset_0-31_0">WDOM&lt;x&gt;, bits [2x+1:2x], for x = 15 to 0:
      </h4><div class="field"><p>Configures the Interrupt Domain that wire ((16 * n) + x) is assigned to.</p>
<p>Programming an Interrupt Domain not supported by the IWB results in <span class="arm-defined-word">CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE</span> behavior with the following options:</p>
<ul>
<li>No signals are generated by the IWB for a wire assigned to an unsupported Interrupt Domain.
</li><li>The wire is treated as being assigned to another supported Interrupt Domain and a read of this field returns the Interrupt Domain the wire is assigned to.
</li></ul>
<p>Access to control fields for wires which are not implemented are RAZ/WI.</p><table class="valuetable"><tr><th>WDOM&lt;x&gt;</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b00</td><td>
          <p>Secure</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b01</td><td>
          <p>Non-secure</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b10</td><td>
          <p>EL3</p>
        </td></tr><tr><td class="bitfield">0b11</td><td>
          <p>Realm</p>
        </td></tr></table><p>The reset behavior of this field is:</p><ul><li>On a GIC reset, 
      this field resets
       to an <span class="arm-defined-word">UNKNOWN</span> value.</li></ul><p>Accessing this field has the following behavior:</p><ul><li>When IsWireDomainRO((n * 16) + x), access to this field
                            is <span class="access_level">RO</span>.
                        </li><li>
                  Otherwise,
                  
                  access to this field
                  is <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
                </li></ul></div><div class="access_mechanisms"><h2>Access Instructions</h2>
        <p>When the Interrupt Domain assigned of a wire is fixed, access to the corresponding field is RO.</p>

      
        <p>This register can only be accessed through the MPPAS of the IWB.</p>
      <p>Accesses to this register use the following encodings:</p><div class="access_block"><p>Accessible at offset <span class="hexnumber">0x8000 + (4 * n)</span> from IWB_CONFIG_FRAME</p></div><ul><li>When IWB_CR0.IDLE == '0', accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RO</span>.
          </li><li>When !IsAccessIWBMPPAS(), accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RAZ/WI</span>.
          </li><li>Otherwise, accesses to this register are <span class="access_level">RW</span>.
          </li></ul><p style="text-align: right">
